Description:
    Copies SagaForge's engine migration into your app's db/migrate (or, for a
    multi-database setup, db/NAME_migrate).

    Safe to re-run: it uses ActiveRecord::Migration.copy, which is idempotent
    (an already-installed migration is skipped, not duplicated).

    With no --database flag, the destination is resolved from SagaForge's own
    configuration (config.database / config.connects_to), so a later run (e.g.
    after a gem upgrade) still lands in the right place without repeating the
    flag.

Example:
    bin/rails generate saga_forge:migrations

    This copies SagaForge's migration into db/migrate.

    bin/rails generate saga_forge:migrations --database=saga

    This copies SagaForge's migration into db/saga_migrate instead.
